Repros without JitStress, and with altjit, when generating:
```
                                                               /--*  t1970  float
Generating: N023 (  5,  8) [001972] UA-----------             *  STORE_LCL_FLD float  V53 tmp1         ud:3->0[+47] Fseq[tmp2] NA REG NA
```

This is a test of struct explicit layout
```
[StructLayout(LayoutKind.Explicit)]
internal struct AA
{
    [FieldOffset(3)]
    public byte tmp1;

    [FieldOffset(8)]
    public float q;

    [FieldOffset(47)]
    public float tmp2;

    public AA(float qq)
    {
        tmp1 = 0;
        tmp2 = 0;
        q = qq;
    }
```

and we're trying to generate `vstr s8, [fp-117]`, but assert that vstr offsets must be 4-byte aligned.

Note that when repro'ing with altjit, first you get:
```
NO_WAY("JIT must expand the intrinsic!");
```
in `System.Runtime.Intrinsics.X86.Sse41:get_IsSupported():bool` before getting to the failure in `TestApp:Main():int`

I don't have a solution yet, because it appeared that for code like
```
[StructLayout(LayoutKind.Explicit)]
internal struct AA {
    [FieldOffset(47)]
    public float tmp2;
    public AA() {
      tmp2 = 0;
    }
```
IL doesn't have `CEE_UNALIGNED` prefix, so we can't catch `GTF_IND_UNALIGNED` because it is not yet set, it will be set later here:
https://github.com/dotnet/runtime/blob/38bef8c60e9483eeb16d85850ad6109c4bc47f5d/src/coreclr/src/jit/morph.cpp#L13075-L13086

@BruceForstall @jashook do you know if IL should have [the unaligned prefix](https://docs.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/system.reflection.emit.opcodes.unaligned?view=netframework-4.8) in this case or not?

It doesn't affect ARM64, because there we need both unaligned and volatile to change instruction and all volatile operations are not transformed by lclmorph.

It is possible to teach `genCodeForStoreLclFld` to work with unaligned fields, but not clear which phase should set this flag on the node.
